|~ `::absent`, the mark in a shape of a key some records lack, and the
   laws declared under it.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence], [QSPTH#shape]. ~|

:absent
  |~~ An absent marks in a shape a part some of the data lacks, a key some
      of the records merged there lack, each key of the records and folds
      an empty map stands beside, `[{:a 1} {:b 2} {}] | shape` answering
      `::shape[#[{:a ::absent::number} {:b ::absent::number}]]`, or the
      element of a vector or a set empty in some, over the shape of the
      rest and outside `::nullable`:
      `[{:a 1} {:a 2 :b "x"}] | shape` answers
      `::shape[{:a ::number :b ::absent::string}]`.
      ::link~(::shape | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ The shape of the part where the data holds it. ~~|
    | proves :marksAKeySomeRecordsLack
        |~~ A key some records lack stands marked absent. ~~|
        ~([{:a 1} {:a 2 :b "x"}] | shape | eq ::shape[{:a ::number :b ::absent::string}])
    | proves :marksEachRecordBesideAnEmptyMap
        |~~ An empty map marks each key of the records beside it absent. ~~|
        ~([{:a 1} {:b 2} {}] | shape | eq ::shape[#[{:a ::absent::number} {:b ::absent::number}]])
    | proves :marksTheElementOfAVectorEmptyInSome
        |~~ The element of a vector empty in some of the data is absent. ~~|
        ~([{:labels [{:name "bug"}]} {:labels []}] | shape | eq ::shape[{:labels [::absent{:name ::string}]}])
    | proves :standsOutsideTheNullMark
        |~~ A key missing from some records and null in others is absent
            outside and nullable within.
        ~~|
        ~([{:a 1} {:a null} {}] | shape | eq ::shape[{:a ::absent::nullable::number}])
